ISO-10303-21;
/* Tfa249: genuine CheckSplittingVertices trigger: face[0] outer wire has edge AB as ONE uninterrupted EDGE_CURVE A(0,0,0)-B(10,0,0) (never pre-split); a separate inner triangle wire (V1-V2-V3) has V1=(5,0,5e-8), a NEW independent VERTEX_POINT that is NOT a topological endpoint of edge AB, offset 5e-8 off AB's interior (within default 1e-7 tolerance, not exactly on it) -- V.IsSame(V1)||V.IsSame(V2) is FALSE for edge AB, unlike the ~17 existing misnamed CheckSplittingVertices/FixSplitFace fixtures which all encode the vertex as a genuine shared topological endpoint; companion 1x1 face ensures shape(1) */
